**measure.hpp derives stick and motion calibration from controller samples.**

## Interface

`stick_measurer` exports `observe_rest(stick_vector) noexcept`, `observe_sweep(stick_vector) noexcept`, `finalize() const noexcept -> stick_calibration`, `reset() noexcept`, `rest_samples() const noexcept -> size_t`, and `sweep_samples() const noexcept -> size_t`.

`motion_bias_measurer` exports `observe(const motion_sample&) noexcept`, `finalize(motion_calibration&) const noexcept`, `reset() noexcept`, and `samples() const noexcept -> size_t`.

## Behavior

`stick_measurer` averages resting vectors for center, tracks sweep extents via `max_x_`/`max_y_`, and guarantees `finalize()` returns a validation-safe, nondegenerate `stick_calibration` without allocation.

`motion_bias_measurer` averages raw gyroscope (`gx_`–`gz_`) and accelerometer (`ax_`–`az_`) readings; `finalize()` writes bias while preserving device-provided scales.

`profile.hpp`, `axis.hpp`, `motion.hpp`, `types.hpp`, and `utility.hpp` define calibration, sample, type, and helper contracts; `reset()` clears accumulators and counts.